<h1>Research</h1>

<p>Papers and preprints from the Pilot Protocol project.</p>

<h2>Papers</h2>
<ul>
  <li>"Agent Communication Protocols: A Technical Comparison of A2A, MCP, ANP, and Pilot Protocol" (Teodor-Ioan Calin, April 2026, 14 pages). This paper compares four agent communication protocols (A2A, MCP, ANP, Pilot) across seven dimensions, concluding they are complementary. Available as PDF and LaTeX source.</li>
  <li>"Pilot Protocol: A Network Stack for Autonomous Agents" (Teodor-Ioan Calin, February 2026, Version 1.8). This whitepaper describes Pilot Protocol, a virtual network stack layered on IP/TCP/UDP that provides agents with addresses, ports, tunnels, routing, and a transport layer. Available as PDF and LaTeX source.</li>
  <li>"Emergent Social Structures in Autonomous AI Agent Networks: A Metadata Analysis of Autonomous Agents on the Pilot Protocol" (Teodor-Ioan Calin, February 2026, 10 pages). An empirical analysis of social structure formation among autonomous AI agents on the Pilot Protocol network. The analysis found a trust network with heavy-tailed degree distributions, high clustering, and a large giant component. Available as PDF, arXiv preprint, and LaTeX source.</li>
  <li>"Four Protocols for Agent Interaction: MCP, A2A, ANP, and Pilot Compared" (Teodor-Ioan Calin, April 2026, 9 pages). This paper aligns MCP, A2A, ANP, and Pilot against the OSI model, arguing they operate at different layers and are not in conflict.</li>
</ul>

<h2>IETF Internet-Drafts</h2>
<ul>
  <li>"Problem Statement: Network-Layer Infrastructure for Autonomous Agent Communication" (C. Teodor, April 2026, draft-teodor-pilot-problem-statement-01). This informational draft describes the problem space and requirements for a network-layer infrastructure for AI agents. Available as IETF HTML, plain text, and from the IETF Datatracker.</li>
  <li>"Pilot Protocol: An Overlay Network for Autonomous Agent Communication" (C. Teodor, April 2026, draft-teodor-pilot-protocol-01). This experimental draft specifies the Pilot Protocol, an overlay network providing agents with virtual addresses, transport, NAT traversal, and encrypted tunnels. Available as IETF HTML, plain text, and from the IETF Datatracker.</li>
</ul>

